<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Qantas up on sentiment change-analysts.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Qantas up on sentiment change-analysts.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A strong rise in Qantas Airways Ltd's share price over the past two months is due to the stock being oversold previously and investors switching to the airline stock after the TNT Ltd takeover, aviation analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;There was a lot of negative sentiment when the stock was driven down to about A$1.80 -- at that price it was a screaming buy,&quot; said one Melbourne-based avaiation analyst, who did not want to be named.</p>
<p>Qantas shares have risen 35 percent over past two months to hit a 10 month high on Tuesday after hitting a record low of A$1.79 on November 6, 1996.</p>
